model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "A native grant without models asks the pool nothing: carry 0681's per-check pool device check and its pool-access refusal apply only to grants with models. A tools-only grant's access checks, token issuance and refreshes, and tool calls are decided by the grant, its consent and token rows and live membership in its tools organization, so they keep working while the pool's control plane fails. A revoked tools-only grant is refused at once by the tools gateway's per-call reads of its tool calls, and by a remembered access answer within carry 0681's 3-second bound. Its access answer's display carries the account and the grant's pool id with an empty name and no pool choices. A tools-only approval never calls the pool's register: the host opens the pool's signed setup intent itself, requires the approving person to be its owner, checks live membership in its organization, and records the policy with the intent's pool and a computer id of 32 hex digits from SHA-256 of the grant id, which can't equal the pool's own UUIDs. It then reports the device to the pool's native control as learn, in the background, and the native devices endpoint lists the person's live tools-only grants for the pool's Connect list to learn any the pool missed. Revoking a tools-only grant tells the pool but succeeds whatever it answers. A grant with models still registers at the pool, asks it on every check, refresh and tool call, and revokes its computer there first; the pool's outage refuses it as unavailable."
    }
  }
}
